## Human setup (outside the terminal)

> These steps cannot be done by the agent. A human must perform them
> and update the ESD `human_setup_steps[].status` when complete.

- [ ] Sign up for an account at the provider
- [ ] Confirm billing setup (if `billing_required: true`)
- [ ] Generate credentials in the provider dashboard
- [ ] Approve OAuth/app permissions (if `oauth_required: true`)
- [ ] Configure domain/DNS (if `domain_dns_required: true`)
- [ ] Pass compliance/legal review (if `compliance_review_required: true`)
- [ ] Decide sandbox vs production tier

## Terminal setup (after credentials are available)

> These steps can run inside the agent once credentials are present.

- [ ] Add required env vars to local `.env` (NAMES ONLY in this repo;
      values stay in `.env`, which must be gitignored)
- [ ] Install provider SDK *only if* the existing routing system
      supports it AND the user has approved
- [ ] Implement adapter for the service
- [ ] Add mock implementation for tests (see `mock_strategy`)
- [ ] Wire ESD events into TRACE
- [ ] Update QA plan with provider-specific checks

